              "conversation_id": "conversation-8e8a2cea-2da4-4785-a474-bd8681e05fd1",
              "role": "tutor",
              "content": "In the course example, the server requires a permitted Origin on state-changing requests. This adds a check of the request\u2019s cross-site context, rather than relying only on the browser\u2019s automatically attached authentication cookie. A valid session identifies the server-side session, while Origin checking helps address whether the request came from an allowed origin; HttpOnly does not provide this protection by itself.\n\nCheck: why would requiring a permitted Origin add information that the session cookie alone does not provide?",
              "action": "answer",
